#   project's copyright notice and the MIT permission notice. Full notices
#   are reproduced in the accompanying xmss-vectors-report.md, section 5.
#
# INDEPENDENT VERIFICATION (2026-08-18)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   Every valid record was verified with a from-scratch RFC 8391 verifier
#   written for this retrieval (xmss_verify.py, kept alongside this file):
#   the root recomputed from (message, signature, SEED) equals the root
#   embedded in the public key. Labels were NOT trusted -- each leaf index
#   below was read out of the first 4 bytes of the signature itself.
#   Structural checks enforced: public key exactly 68 bytes with OID
#   00000001; signature exactly 2500 bytes.
#   Controls that DID fire: one-byte flip in the WOTS+ signature, rewriting
#   the idx field to 0, and altering the message all produce a mismatch.
#   Cross-check: on the post-quantum-cryptography/KAT sigVer set the
#   verifier independently reproduced the published expected results on all
#   10 cases (1 valid, 9 invalid), agreeing case for case.
#
# FORMAT
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   Valid = 1 (verifies) or 0 (MUST be rejected -- see the final section)
#   Msg = <lowercase hex, may be empty>
#   PublicKey = <136 hex: OID 00000001 || 32-byte root || 32-byte SEED>
#   Signature = <5000 hex: 4-byte big-endian idx || 32-byte r ||
#                2144-byte WOTS+ sig (67 x 32) || 320-byte auth path (10 x 32)>
#   Where a source appended the message to the signature (ACVP: 2628 bytes),
#   the trailing message was stripped; equality with Msg was checked first.
# ============================================================================

